Gold Intelligence Engine
========================

This application consumes only free, publicly reachable data sources. No
credentials, API keys or paid subscriptions are required or embedded.

Attribution
-----------

U.S. Department of the Treasury — Daily Treasury Par Yield Curve Rates and
  Daily Treasury Par Real Yield Curve Rates. Public domain.
  https://home.treasury.gov

U.S. Commodity Futures Trading Commission — Commitments of Traders.
  Public domain.
  https://publicreporting.cftc.gov

Federal Reserve Bank of New York — Reference Rates (SOFR, EFFR). Public domain.
  https://markets.newyorkfed.org

Cboe Global Markets, Inc. — delayed index and equity quotes and daily history.
  Data is delayed and is used under attribution. (c) Cboe Global Markets, Inc.
  https://www.cboe.com

European Central Bank — euro foreign exchange reference rates, retrieved via
  the Frankfurter API. Attribution required.
  https://www.ecb.europa.eu / https://frankfurter.app

gold-api.com — spot gold and silver reference prices. Attribution required.
  https://api.gold-api.com

Yahoo Finance chart API — optional provider for the dated COMEX futures curve.
  https://query1.finance.yahoo.com

TradingView public scanner — index, futures and open-interest quotes.
  https://scanner.tradingview.com

Kraken — PAXG/USD order book, spread and daily candles (1 PAXG = 1 fine ounce).
  https://api.kraken.com

OKX — XAUT/USDT order book and daily candles.
  https://www.okx.com

Swissquote — public OTC bid/ask quotes for XAU/USD by size tier.
  https://forex-data-feed.swissquote.com

World Gold Council — LBMA-based benchmark price series.
  https://fsapi.gold.org

U.S. Bureau of Labor Statistics — CPI and unemployment series, public API v1.
  https://api.bls.gov

ForexFactory / FairEconomy — economic calendar with consensus forecasts.
  https://nfs.faireconomy.media

Shanghai Gold Exchange Au(T+D) quote, via Sina and Eastmoney public endpoints.
  https://hq.sinajs.cn / https://push2.eastmoney.com

Source policy
-------------

Every source in the stack is reachable without an API key, an account, or a
paid subscription. Each published value carries its source, licence class,
retrieval timestamp and quality tier in the data contract, and that provenance
is rendered next to the value. Attribution is given above; no additional
publication restriction is applied to any value.

Disclaimer
----------

This software produces a statistical description of market conditions. It is
not investment advice, it does not publish a calibrated probability until a
live scoring record exists, and it reports the absence of a source rather than
substituting a guess.
